# CSS Standards

Foundation/Domaine conventions only. For generic modern-CSS reference (container queries, cascade layers, logical properties, `:is()`/`:where()`, view transitions, `prefers-reduced-motion`, property order, performance), use [MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS).

## Tailwind v4 First

Style with Tailwind v4 utilities by default. Tokens come from the `@meetdomaine/project-syrah-config` package and the `@theme` blocks in `src/styles/@theme.css` and `@colors.css` (spacing, colors, radius, fonts, button variables). Never hardcode arbitrary values (`bg-[#fff]`, `p-[24px]`) when a token utility exists.

Write custom CSS only for: keyframe animations, vendor hacks (`-webkit-appearance`), Liquid-driven runtime variables, third-party overrides, or pseudo-selectors Tailwind can't express.

Use mobile-first responsive prefixes (`md:`, `lg:`). Put custom CSS in `{% stylesheet %}` blocks, never `{% style %}` (reserve `{% style %}` for runtime Liquid values only).

### Semantic token utilities

Use the design-system token utilities, not raw values:

- Color: `bg-background`, `bg-background-secondary`, `text-foreground`, `text-foreground-inverse`, `text-foreground-secondary`, `border-border-01`, `border-border-02`, `bg-accent-01`, `bg-accent-02`, `text-link`, `bg-danger`, `text-focus`.
- Spacing scale (`none 2xs xs sm md lg xl 2xl 3xl`): `p-md`, `gap-y-sm`, `pt-lg`, `py-(--section-padding)`.
- Page grid: `px-pagemargin`, `pagegutter`, `pagecolumns`.
- Radius: `rounded-sm`, `rounded-md`, `rounded-rounded`. Max-width: `max-w-md` etc.

### @utility for repeated patterns

Create an `@utility` (with `@apply`) only for patterns reused across components — see the existing `text-body`, `text-caption`, `text-heading-*`, `utility`, `caption` utilities in `src/styles/`. Don't wrap a single-use class set.

```css
@utility btn {
  @apply uppercase tracking-[0.05em] px-6 py-3 rounded-full transition-colors;
}
```

## Custom CSS

### Specificity

- No IDs as selectors. Avoid bare element selectors.
- Avoid `!important`; if unavoidable, comment why inline.
- Target `0,1,0` (a single `.class`). Cap at `0,4,0` for unavoidable parent/child chains (pseudo-classes like `:hover` may force this).
- Keep selectors readable at a glance.

### BEM naming

- Block = component (`.product-card`). Element = `block__element` (`.product-card__title`). Modifier = `block--modifier` / `block__element--modifier`.
- Separate words with single dashes (`.product-card__multi-word-element`).
- One element segment per classname — never `__wrapper__button`. If an element could stand alone, start a new block scope.
- The block namespace must wrap its elements; never use an element class as a parent of its block.
- A modifier (`--x`) always needs the base class present: `class="button button--secondary"`, never `button--secondary` alone or `button button-secondary`.
- Keep modifiers on the highest element that makes sense for extensibility.
- Global `@utility` classes are the exception — they don't follow BEM and assume no block.

## CSS Variables

Prefer Tailwind utilities. Use CSS variables for Liquid-driven runtime values, global theme customization, or third-party APIs.

### Where global variables live

Global `:root` variables are defined across:

- `src/styles/@theme.css` and `src/styles/@colors.css` — build-time design tokens inside `@theme {}` (spacing, color, radius, fonts, button variables).
- `snippets/@color-schemes.liquid` — per-scheme color/button overrides on `:root` and `.color-{{ scheme.id }}`.
- `snippets/@system-colors.liquid` — global system colors on `:root` (`--color-danger`, `--color-focus`, etc.).

(There is no `snippets/theme-styles-variables.liquid`.)

### Scoping & namespacing

- Scope component variables to the component; scoped vars may reference globals.
- Namespace variable names to avoid collisions (`--component-padding`, not `--padding`) unless intentional bleed-through.

```css
.facets {
  --drawer-padding: var(--spacing-md);
  --facets-open-z-index: 4;
}
```

### Scope section/block instances inline, not by id selector

Reset variable values via an inline `style=""` attribute driven by settings. Avoid the `.selector--{{ block.id }}` pattern — it keeps CSS out of Liquid `{% style %}` and cuts selector redundancy.

```html
<!-- ✅ -->
<section style="--background-color: {{ settings.background_color }}; --padding: {{ settings.padding }}px;">…</section>

<!-- ❌ -->
{% style %} .selector--{{ block.id }} { --button-color: {{ settings.button_color }}; } {% endstyle %}
<button class="selector--{{ block.id }}">…</button>
```

Use variables to cut property-assignment redundancy across modifiers:

```css
.button { background: rgb(var(--button-color) / 0.75); }
.button--secondary { --button-color: var(--secondary-color); }
```

## CSS Nesting

- No `&` except for a direct relationship: state selectors (`&:hover`, `&:focus`) or interacting modifiers (`.button--integrated { &.button--text }`).
- Never nest beyond the first level.
- Nest media queries even when there's nothing to override yet, so additions don't require flipping the query inside.
- You may nest child overrides under a parent modifier when one parent state drives several children (avoids repeating `parent--full-width` on each child) — still one level only.
